# Jupyter notebooks are checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# Notebooks are stored LF in the repo, like everything else. On a Windows
# checkout `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites them to CRLF on disk, and the
# `mixed-line-ending` pre-commit hook then rewrites them straight back to LF —
# so a single `pre-commit run --all-files` leaves every notebook in the tree
# looking modified. The diffs are empty (`git diff --numstat` reports nothing),
# but `git status` shows 200+ dirty files, which is easy to mistake for real
# work and easy to sweep into a commit by accident.
#
# Pinning the checkout to LF removes the disagreement: jupyter and nbformat
# already write LF, so the hook has nothing left to fix. This changes only how
# the file is written into the working tree — the stored blobs are already LF
# and are untouched, so no renormalisation happens and no diff is produced.
*.ipynb text eol=lf
